WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.990 --> 00:00:06.890
It's hard to believe that Adam Sandler was
once one of the most successful comedy actors

00:00:06.890 --> 00:00:08.010
in Hollywood.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:11.060
But since his glory days, Sandler has tumbled
pretty hard.

00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.639
In flop after flop, his career appears beyond
repair.

00:00:14.639 --> 00:00:18.890
What's really behind Sandler's stagnant trajectory?

00:00:18.890 --> 00:00:20.539
Costly and Crappy

00:00:20.539 --> 00:00:25.199
The infamous Sony hacks from 2014 revealed
that Sandler was regarded by many studio executives

00:00:25.199 --> 00:00:26.830
as a waste of money.

00:00:26.830 --> 00:00:27.930
One Sony employee wrote:

00:00:27.930 --> 00:00:32.509
"We continue to be saddled with mundane, formulaic
Adam Sandler films."

00:00:32.509 --> 00:00:36.120
Another exec said that Sandler's excessive
private jet usage on the studio's dime was

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:37.680
"stressing [him] out."

00:00:37.680 --> 00:00:42.290
He went on to detail trips of Sandler's costing
in excess of $68,000 a flight.

00:00:42.290 --> 00:00:47.410
Perhaps, suggested the executive, Netflix—with
whom Sandler had recently partnered—could

00:00:47.410 --> 00:00:51.550
share the costs of the failing star's offices
on the lot, which ran the studio $2 million

00:00:51.550 --> 00:00:52.550
a year.

00:00:52.550 --> 00:00:53.860
Then again, maybe not...

00:00:53.860 --> 00:00:56.800
Netflix's Regrets

00:00:56.800 --> 00:01:00.990
Sandler's first release of his four-picture
deal with Netflix, The Ridiculous 6, garnered

00:01:00.990 --> 00:01:03.530
publicity in all the wrong ways.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:07.320
During filming, a dozen Native American actors
walked off-set after hearing what they felt

00:01:07.320 --> 00:01:08.890
were racist jokes.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:12.420
But when it was finally released, the movie
actually set a record as the most-watched

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.710
film on Netflix within its first 30 days.

00:01:14.710 --> 00:01:19.700
Then again, the film was harshly criticized
for what many saw as its racist concept and

00:01:19.700 --> 00:01:20.700
undertones.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:27.920
The Ridiculous 6 managed to score a ridiculous
0% on Rotten Tomatoes.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:30.369
Print is Dead...To Him

00:01:30.369 --> 00:01:34.680
Sandler himself doesn't seem interested in
challenging his unfavorable media portrayal.

00:01:34.680 --> 00:01:38.380
After press junkets for Billy Madison, he
apparently read some unfavorable descriptions

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:42.520
of himself and decided to stop talking to
print journalists altogether—an arrangement

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.679
no one really seems to mind.

00:01:44.679 --> 00:01:48.780
These days, Sandler's Twitter feed, perhaps
his best means of reaching fans, is hardly

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:50.010
engaging.

00:01:50.010 --> 00:01:51.600
No Ladies' Man

00:01:51.600 --> 00:01:54.700
Sandler has also earned a bad marks for his
portrayals and relationships with women in

00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:55.700
Hollywood.

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:00.051
In June of 2016, actress Rose McGowan tweeted
out a casting notice she'd received for one

00:02:00.051 --> 00:02:04.429
of Sandler's movies that encouraged women
auditioning to wear "form-fitting tanks that

00:02:04.429 --> 00:02:07.889
show off cleavage—push-up bras encouraged."

00:02:07.889 --> 00:02:11.390
Soon after calling out Sandler on Twitter,
McGowan said she was fired by her agent, and

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:13.250
a social media outcry erupted.

00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:17.971
Meanwhile, at a premiere for Hotel Transylvania
2, he and co-star Kevin James, both in what

00:02:17.971 --> 00:02:22.220
appeared to be gym clothes, were photographed
next to a very dressed-up Selena Gomez.

00:02:22.220 --> 00:02:26.110
The images sparked a debate online about double
standards for men and women in Hollywood.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:29.680
And seriously, c'mon guys—you don't own
shirts with buttons?

00:02:29.680 --> 00:02:32.760
Sandler may have played a girl in Jack and
Jill, but he doesn't seem to relate well with

00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:33.260
them.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:33.760
“Ow!

00:02:33.760 --> 00:02:34.900
Oh my god!”

00:02:35.240 --> 00:02:36.400
Stale Co-Stars

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:41.110
Comedy posses are no new phenomena, especially
among SNL alumni.

00:02:41.110 --> 00:02:44.940
But Sandler's insistence on working time and
again with actors like David Spade, Kevin

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:49.130
James, and Rob Schneider may be preventing
him from reaching younger fans.

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:53.090
He did hire Natasha Leggero for his Netflix
release The Do-Over, but relegated her to

00:02:53.090 --> 00:02:57.730
a supporting "crazy wife" role, leaving the
more substantial acting to David Spade.

00:02:57.730 --> 00:03:02.170
In the case of The Do-Over, this resulted
in yet another slew of disastrous reviews.

00:03:02.170 --> 00:03:04.660
But hey, at least it earned higher praise
than his previous outing!

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:08.880
Where The Ridiculous 6 had a mind-boggling
0% on Rotten Tomatoes, The Do-Over blows it

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.620
out of the water with...a five percent.

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:16.730
“I award you no points, and may god have
mercy on your soul.”

00:03:16.730 --> 00:03:18.110
Thanks for watching!

00:03:18.110 --> 00:03:20.830
Subscribe to our YouTube channel to watch
more videos like the one you just saw.

00:03:20.830 --> 00:03:23.980
And leave us a comment to let us know why
you think Adam Sandler's career isn't what

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:24.590
it used to be…

